<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 75,573 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 75,573 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 75,573 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Sunday, compared to 65,631 tonnes on in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Sunday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			22,328	   15,214</p>
<p>    Import cargo			53,245	   50,417</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, two ships were expected to sail and six were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>Tallow		    3,137	 Alam Karang	30/12</p>
<p>Palm oil		 18,000	 Wawasan Courage    1/1</p>
<p>High-speed diesel    56,000	 Al-Maqwa	     due</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Bunga Selasih    28/12</p>
<p>Crude oil		67,600	 Stravos-1	  27/12</p>
<p>Furnace oil	    42,000	 Trade Resolve    25/12</p>
<p>Soybean oil	    5,350	  Champion Trader  25/12</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
